      "body": "\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>app/src/main/java/de/lukasneugebauer/nextcloudcookbook/core/util/OkHttpClientProvider.kt (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `78-80`: _🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n> \n> **Log the TLS configuration failure.**\n> \n> The catch block silently falls back to the default client. This prevents diagnosis when a self-signed server cannot connect. Keep the fallback, but log the exception with `Timber`.\n> \n> Based on learnings, use `Timber` for all logging and do not define a manual `TAG` constant.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Proposed change</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  } catch (e: Exception) {\n> -    // Do nothing if SSL configuration fails, keep default settings\n> +    Timber.e(e, \"Could not configure trust-all TLS\")\n>  }\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\n> rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n> \n> In\n> `@app/src/main/java/de/lukasneugebauer/nextcloudcookbook/core/util/OkHttpClientProvider.kt`\n> around lines 78 - 80, Update the exception handler around the TLS configuration\n> in OkHttpClientProvider to log the caught exception with Timber, while\n> preserving the fallback to default settings. Use Timber directly and do not\n> introduce a manual TAG constant.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <!-- cr-comment:v1:56354735523beaa3448bab92 -->\n> \n> _Sources: Learnings, Linters/SAST tools_\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a bri